 {:seon.task/name "spend-has-a-render"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: every paid model request is a fact, a model-call entity holding its agent, its :seon.model-call/tokens and the cache-hit and cache-miss counts; a request's budget key is its agent's id unless one is named (seon.agent-proc). So what an agent has spent is the sum over its model calls, a value derived from its pull and computed where it is read, never stored (docs/decisions.md, 2026-11-11: no derived value is stored). The effect owner, seon.fx, keeps the same sum in its proc's state (:spent {budget-key amount}) to admit a request in one read and refuses one past its budget (:seon.fx/budget-spent); that counter is no entity's data, no pull holds it, and a render is never handed it. Nothing shows spend: the page sums the run's tokens only.

The change: spend is drawn from an entity's pull. (1) The agent's pattern asks :seon.model-call/tokens in its model-call join (resources/seon/schemas/seon.facts.edn, the :seon.db/agent-fact pattern: one clause). (2) A render of an agent's pulled calls draws what it has spent, as a part of the agent's page, the same hiccup for the person and the model; it reads nothing but the pull (docs/render.md#a-render-does-no-work-of-its-own). No budget is drawn: no config key holds a spend budget today (task seon.model/budgets-are-data-and-spend-is-measured makes one), so the part says spent and nothing of a limit. Root's page is not asked to show it: root draws each agent as an entry from a join that holds no model calls, and widening that join would pull every agent's calls into root's page (found by a Seon agent preparing this task, 2026-11-11).

Not covered, and said on the page as absent rather than shown as zero: a charged request that is not an agent's model call (an embedding call; the judge's, whose cost is inside :seon.judge/score) has no entity of its own, and a running agent's calls are on its branch until it merges, so main cannot sum them before the one merge's sync.

Proof: seon.render-test/spend-reads-by-its-render (an agent's pull holding two model calls with tokens renders their sum in the hiccup and in what the model reads; an agent with no call renders no spend). A render is tested as seon.render-test/the-problem-report-reads-by-class tests the problem report's."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/spend-reads-by-its-render}}
 {:seon.task/name "namespace-agent-debug-and-data-pages"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.web/handler` serves root's page, /root/debug, /agent/<key>/<id> with its /ctx and /debug tabs (debug is the raw wire: docs/render.md#the-debug-page-is-the-wire-request) and POST /call. v1's route table (~/src/seon/src/seon/render/route.clj) also served /ns/{namespace} and /ns/{namespace}/debug and /data (docs/parity.md). Missing: the owner cannot see a namespace's vars, contracts and the tests reaching them, or main's data. Correct: each a view the render proc renders from main's or the agent's branch, through renders declared on the values' schemas (docs/render.md), routed beside /agent/; read first what each v1 page showed and keep what the owner acts on. Replaces nothing."
  :seon.task/kind :work
