 {:seon.task/name "an-agent-spawned-with-a-task-keeps-its-branch-on-main"
  :seon.task/plan "Seen 2026-11-06, and narrower than first filed: `seon.system/observed` leaves an agent on a task's branch to its start's fact (`seon.task/start-tx`, written by the reconciler and by attach), so a real run is fine. Only a hand-typed `(seon.system/spawn! sys {:task t :branch :b})`, which no start follows, leaves main with no :seon.agent/branch, and its debug tab then says `no model turn yet` after a model turn its branch records. Make a page that can't read an agent's branch say that rather than that nothing happened; then `spawn!` with :task either writes the start or refuses."
