ng: four seon.render-cost-test proofs are 1-6% over their call bounds (a-change-costs-its-components 3,720 calls against 3,660; the-printer-renders-nested-values-in-one-pass 422 against 400; a-restart-draws-its-turns-in-one-walk 3,421 against 3,400; a-member-gone-costs-the-lists-lookups), because seon.render/schema-of now calls seon.db/most-specific for every map (before, only for an entity with two identity attributes) and emit calls seon.render/entity-render for every view: fold the lookups into one uncontracted step in emit, or a single lookup by the index's :entity-schemas a key, and measure again; a bound moves only with the owner's yes. Also red: seon.main-test/no-docstring-carries-a-date (a docstring this branch wrote: find and fix). (b) fixed on jolt/walk-2a (839e8318df): the model output's work (the lookup of an entity's model render, the placing closure, the children held once) runs only in a component run of a walk that asks for :seon.render/wire, never on a cache hit; schema-of keeps a single owning schema a lookup with no call and recognizes a rendered schema by the index's :drawn-schemas (now every entity schema that declares a render, not only identity ones); a view is never an element's attributes by a type check with no contracted call. seon.render-cost-test, seon.db-test and the 2a proof are green, no bound moved; the docstrings cite undated sections. What still reds its prove: root's entity reads as the config (cause (a)), waiting on the config entity. Later on jolt/walk-2a (tip 5d205af272): seon.render/render-pull (pull db f ix outputs [opts]), a pull rendered in one pass and let go, how a past point is read; its root may be a model output's call (opts {:seon.render/as :seon.render/wire}), whose answer is the model output, each entity it places rendered by its own :seon.render/wire, and a call's answer wins over the root entity's own model render. Context's 2b is on jolt/model-wire-2a (caf7f678c1), built from walk-2a's tip with no spike: its byte